00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:18.750
By the time I received this warning note,
it was already gone.

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:21.550
Is it the Dynamite Bombers again?

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:24.910
They're quite old-fashioned to use gridded writing paper.

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:26.510
I won't let them get away next time.

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:33.440
Be that as it may, you still can't give us the stone until you catch them.

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:37.800
If you can get it back, I will keep my end of the bargain.

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:43.030
It's all your fault.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:45.860
Damn you, Dynamite Bombers!

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:46.930
Welcome to Tokyo

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:48.620
Out wit'em passports.
Welcome to Tokyo

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:54.000
Y'all ain't no Dynamite Bombers, are ya?

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.350
Who?

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:58.380
They're the ones that made a whole mess o' things not more'n six months ago,

00:08:58.380 --> 00:09:02.880
an' they went an' lifted the knight squad cap'n's precious thing from unner 'er nose this very mornin',

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:04.860
so everyone's on pin 'n' needles.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:06.890
I thought nobody had accents in Tokyo...

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:13.040
Most checkpoint workers are hired from countries with no vested interest in the area.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:14.140
That so?

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:15.510
So what's a knight squad?

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:16.650
This.

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:16.690
Knights of the Twin Towers
Thunderoad

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:19.840
Y'all call'em Knights of the Twin Towers.

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:26.200
They're the state vigilantes keepin' the peace in this here Always Comima!

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:29.160
Wow! Is this captain strong?

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:32.910
'Course she is. She's a Best with backbone,

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:36.420
even though she's a small, cute girl.

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:45.820
It's kinda hot here...

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:48.930
Strange cloud.

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:51.810
That's called the Comima Cloud
Comima Cloud

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:55.400
I heard that it came from the heat of people

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:57.810
gathering for a festival non-stop, year-round.

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:02.820
In the past, it was apparently only held in that building.

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:05.910
I can see why some people would run away.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:08.160
It's kinda cute though.

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:17.330
Nozomi, look at that!

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:17.910
Huh?

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:22.290
Oh! Chi, let's go!

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:26.550
Excuse me!

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:30.480
Where'd you get that heart-shaped stone?

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:31.140
Stone?

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:33.710
Oh, you mean the security charm?

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:36.350
You can buy them pretty much anywhere.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:38.770
Security charm?

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:40.820
Looks like I was mistaken.

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:42.220
I'm sorry.

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:45.480
It's all right. Chi, let me see your stone.

00:10:45.970 --> 00:10:48.480
We're looking for these.

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:49.780
Have you seen them before?

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:57.260
What's going on?!

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:59.490
They're here! The Dynamite Bombers!

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:00.000
What?!

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:15.600
So, you lot are the Dynamite Bombers?

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:16.390
We're not.

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:19.310
Why do you threaten the peace of Comima?

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:21.100
Do you think this is a game?

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:24.200
How big is your organization? Where's your hideout?

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:25.650
How would we know?

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:29.130
All you've done since the bombing is send us warnings.

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:31.310
Why haven't you acted on them?

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:32.610
We don't know.

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:35.620
I see they've trained you well.

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:36.740
We haven't been trained!

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:41.620
Then when and how did you steal this Drom Berserker?

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:43.460
My Core!

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:48.630
I don't know if you did this to mess with me or the Knights, but it's not a toy—

00:11:48.630 --> 00:11:49.930
We didn't steal it!

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:51.930
That's Chi's stone!

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:56.360
We only just arrived in Tokyo, right?

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:57.640
Uh, right.

00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:59.800
We are investigating your claims,

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:01.420
but even if you aren't the perpetrators,

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:05.200
being caught in possession of this stone has already exposed you as their comrade.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:07.760
We already told you we aren't!

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:10.280
Stop being a bully and give it back!

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:13.150
Look, you're strong, right?

00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:15.110
Let me be your disciple.

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:15.910
What?

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:18.820
I wanna be a drifter Best.

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:21.660
Let's say you'll take me if I manage to land a single finger on you.

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:23.600
Sounds like fun.

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:28.800
If you succeed, forget disciple—
I'll call you master and return this stone.

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:29.910
All right!

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:31.010
Wait, Ai!

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:40.140
I just don't get it.

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:43.140
<i>What would Masami do?</i>

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.400
Give that stone back!

00:12:47.020 --> 00:12:48.200
Nope, can't do it.

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:55.030
Hey, are you sure your stone was stolen?

00:12:55.030 --> 00:12:57.400
How do you know you didn't lose it?

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:58.280
What are you saying?

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:02.760
I'll look for it!

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:05.170
Shut your beak, Garm!

00:13:06.250 --> 00:13:08.170
Where would you even start?

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:10.510
I don't know, but...

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:12.510
You'll collapse in the middle of the street.

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:15.580
But that's Chi's stone.

00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:19.930
Instead of fulfilling her request,
I got her only one stolen instead.

00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:21.060
I can't leave it like this.

00:13:21.490 --> 00:13:22.690
Request?

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:26.730
As my first client, she wanted me to gather these stones for her.

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:30.820
Oh, by the way, I'm taking jobs in place of Maccha Green.

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.890
Maccha Green.

00:13:32.890 --> 00:13:35.000
The infamous peacebroker?

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:38.070
I've heard that she takes jobs through the Tokorozawa president's office.

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:41.510
She even takes on personal jobs like this?

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:48.330
Then you two are also here for that Maccha whatcha-macallit?

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:51.210
Huh? Oh, um...

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:54.420
No, not in particular.

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:57.130
I'm just coming along for the ride.

00:13:57.130 --> 00:13:57.760
Yeah.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:02.380
Very well. Go ahead and look for it.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:03.290
Really?

00:14:03.890 --> 00:14:05.600
You have until sundown.

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:09.770
If you can find my stone by then, I will return this to you.

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:14.230
However, if you do not find it

00:14:15.800 --> 00:14:17.450
four heads will roll.

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:21.270
Roll?

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:27.580
If you're going to worry this much, why did you let her go?

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:34.340
'Cause she's almost at the phase where daddy's little girl starts hating daddy...

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:37.620
I need all the points I can get before that happens.

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:38.840
You're hopeless.

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:42.250
I can't believe you let her out into the world for that.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:45.130
<i>I</i> can't believe you're fine with it, Hina!

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:46.780
What if Nozomi needs her daddy right n—

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:47.600
Stop it.
What if Nozomi needs her daddy right n—

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:48.580
Stop it.

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:54.540
We both supported her decision to help people in Masami's place.

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:57.490
