Why are you being so stubborn, anyway?

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:18.520
Because I told myself

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:22.110
that I'd do my best in her place.

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:29.310
But this place is just too big!

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:31.310
It's not like we have any leads.

00:16:31.310 --> 00:16:32.470
Bushy bush.

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:36.090
Chiaya, what?

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:38.380
That's what the crow said.

00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:40.690
"Inside bushy bush."

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:42.420
"Red."

00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:47.390
Hey, Chi, why do you want to gather those rocks?

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:51.350
Because... they're pretty.

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:53.310
That's it?

00:16:53.310 --> 00:16:55.760
You might have to give up on that one.

00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:59.690
No! As Maccha Green's substitute, I won't let you do that.

00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:02.600
<i>We're</i> not substitutes though.

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:04.570
Anyway, the sun's setting, you know?

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:09.450
There's no sign of their friends.

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:15.460
I found it!

00:17:32.850 --> 00:17:34.850
Here is the agent's recovery fee.

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:39.330
There is one case where the owner is overcharging since the stone is dear to her,

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:41.450
pushing the total fee way over budget—

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:42.980
We'll pay it.

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:44.760
There's no time.

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:47.490
We still don't have enough.

00:17:47.490 --> 00:17:50.960
We had such high hopes for Maccha Green too.

00:17:52.850 --> 00:17:57.490
Yes, requiring these stones as payment for her assistance was a great idea.

00:17:58.270 --> 00:18:02.270
Let's hide that she's beyond recovery and have the clients to send stones first.

00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:04.870
Very well...

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:09.000
You thought me contemptible just now, didn't you?

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:10.300
No, ma'am.

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:14.400
I understand the circumstances.

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:19.470
You should have a meal with your daughter sometime.

00:18:19.470 --> 00:18:21.930
She always seems so lonely.

00:18:21.930 --> 00:18:26.450
You're right. I must talk to her about this soon.

00:18:40.020 --> 00:18:45.560
Very well. I will buy your stone for 100,000 Comima.

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:47.200
It's a deal!

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:50.450
Once I've officially resigned from the squad, I'll contact—

00:18:57.230 --> 00:18:58.850
To the foolish participants of Comima:
In order to fix this rotten festival, we,
the Dynamite Bombers, will place a bomb...

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:04.580
Mr. Momiyama! Will you wait until I catch the Dynamite Bombers?

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:10.490
Final Clearance!!

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:12.990
Excuse me!

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:16.160
I'd like to buy this.

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:16.800
Huh?

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:18.750
I was waiting for the price to go down!

00:19:19.110 --> 00:19:20.780
Sure thing.

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:23.380
How about I let you have it for 50,000 Comima?

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:25.380
Wow! Really?

00:19:25.380 --> 00:19:26.590
W-Wait a minute!

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:29.260
I'll pay 80,000 Comima.

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:31.490
Oh, um...

00:19:31.490 --> 00:19:34.180
Then I'll pay 90,000 Comima!

00:19:34.180 --> 00:19:35.650
Then 100,000!

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:36.510
110,000!

00:19:36.510 --> 00:19:39.490
Uh... then... 120,000!

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:40.490
150,000!

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:43.110
Uh... 1... 16...

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:44.980
180,000 Comima!

00:19:46.570 --> 00:19:48.610
200,000 Comima!

00:19:49.420 --> 00:19:50.700
<i>Wait, don't tell me...</i>

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:53.000
<i>She's with him?!</i>

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:08.710
Garm, how did you get out of your cage again?

00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:13.960
My stone! How did it get in there?

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:15.510
Damn bird is messing with me.

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:19.760
Wait...

00:20:20.310 --> 00:20:22.770
This is my fault?

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:32.600
Thanks for your business!

00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:35.910
It's night already...

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:39.450
Do you think the "four heads"
she mentioned are ours?

00:20:39.450 --> 00:20:42.980
I doubt they would send us to the guillotine for steal—

00:20:42.980 --> 00:20:45.270
We didn't steal anything!

00:20:45.270 --> 00:20:49.180
Yeah, but she doesn't believe us! That's why we're in this mess in the first place!

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:50.960
I know, but...

00:20:52.670 --> 00:20:56.680
Hey, how about we escape now and come back later?

00:20:56.680 --> 00:20:58.050
Later?

00:20:58.050 --> 00:21:00.430
Yep! We'll get stronger and come back!

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:05.270
We'll kick that captain's butt, and get Chi's stone back!

00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:06.690
Let's do this!

00:21:07.270 --> 00:21:09.000
Who's doing the kicking?

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:09.730
Me.

00:21:10.110 --> 00:21:12.380
How will you get stronger?

00:21:12.380 --> 00:21:13.860
Train somewhere!

00:21:13.860 --> 00:21:19.670
Um, I'd like to escape as much as the next girl,
but they have our passports,

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:21.530
and we have no idea where our motorcycles are.

00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:22.930
We can figure that out later!

00:21:22.930 --> 00:21:24.000
No, we can't!
We can figure that out later!

00:21:24.410 --> 00:21:27.650
Besides, I don't want to run away if we're innocent.

00:21:27.650 --> 00:21:29.500
I didn't say we'd run away.

00:21:29.500 --> 00:21:32.310
Maybe if we ask for one more day...

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:35.180
If it was really stolen by those Dynamite Bombers,

00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:38.760
not even <i>ten</i> years would be enough to find it!

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:42.690
Wh-What should we do?

00:21:44.020 --> 00:21:46.890
Nonsuke, Yukippe, Uu,

00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:48.760
I'm hungry.

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:55.780
Come with me.

00:21:55.780 --> 00:21:57.780
T-To be executed?!

00:22:02.200 --> 00:22:03.910
Wh-What are you doing?

00:22:04.470 --> 00:22:07.790
Hurry up. I won't hurt you.

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:11.250
They certainly are both real,

00:22:11.250 --> 00:22:13.580
but how do you have two?

00:22:13.580 --> 00:22:17.330
I was wondering if I could receive the payment in advance...

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:19.690
Has the situation changed?

00:22:19.690 --> 00:22:20.690
Yes.

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:24.970
It's not that I don't trust you, but I cannot do that.

00:22:25.960 --> 00:22:28.510
We have pressing matters on our end as well.

00:22:28.510 --> 00:22:31.730
In fact, we would appreciate it if you would give me both stones right now.

00:22:32.730 --> 00:22:38.820
If you insist on waiting until after you eradicate the Dynamite Bombers, then the price—

00:22:38.820 --> 00:22:42.420
no, the whole agreement—must be reconsidered.

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:43.330
Oh, no!

00:22:59.360 --> 00:23:00.800
Take them!

00:23:12.310 --> 00:23:17.490
Thou shalt not pass

00:23:17.780 --> 00:23:22.870
Laws, reason, nobody is getting past

00:23:23.200 --> 00:23:28.700
I don't care what you say

00:23:28.700 --> 00:23:34.170
I'm not letting friends and lovers in either

00:23:34.880 --> 00:23:38.300
My only companion

00:23:39.630 --> 00:23:44.050
is the faint moonlight

00:23:45.140 --> 00:23:55.980
I'm now sitting in the cockpit

00:23:55.980 --> 00:24:02.240
of the black shadow

00:24:02.240 --> 00:24:05.870
deep in the white moon

00:24:28.890 --> 00:24:31.890
You've probably already realized, but this show is a work of fiction.
Any resemblance to real people, groups, or laws is coincidental.
